    "site_desc": "The Twitchell East End Burn site is a new site adjacent to (690m south of) the long term East End Wetland (US-Tw4) site.  This new site was established to measure the recovery of the wetland after a Indigenous prescribed fire on a 32acre (13ha) plot.  The site was burned on 2026-02-27.  There was a large accumulation (~2m) of above ground litter removed by the burn.  This site and the surrounding region are part of the San Joaquin - Sacramento River Delta drained beginning in the 1850's and subsequently used for agriculture. The site was previously an alfalfa field.  The Twitchell Island East End Habitat Restoration Project restored approximately 740 acres of palustrine emergent wetlands with construction in May-November of 2013.",
